<title>USA: Ford files shelf offering for $2 bln in debt.</title>
<headline>Ford files shelf offering for $2 bln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co said Thursday it filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission for a combined offering of up to $2 billion in debt securities.</p>
<p>Of the total offering, Ford previously registered $211,700,000 in debt securities, the filing said. This new registration is for $1,788,300,000.</p>
<p>Ford said net proceeds from the securities will be used for general corporate purposes of Ford or its affiliates.</p>
